            <ArticleTitle>Lead poisoning in an electrician: a bad substitute for a bad habit.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>23-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An electrician presented with a four-month history of unexplained abdominal pain and constipation, which had prompted four hospital admissions and numerous investigations. Blood-film results suggested lead poisoning, and an occupational history revealed that he had chewed about a metre of electrical cable (which contains lead) daily for 10 years as a substitute for smoking.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
